1.
 Image with Links
Create an HTML page where clicking on an image redirects the user to another website or page.
Use the <a> tag to wrap the <img> tag.
Add multiple linked images with different destinations.


2.

Requirements
Page Title and Introduction:

Add a heading (<h1>) as the title of the blog, e.g., "Adventurer's Travel Blog."
Include a brief introductory paragraph under the title to welcome visitors.
Featured Image:

Add a large, visually appealing image (<img> tag) of a famous travel destination.
Use the alt attribute to describe the image (e.g., "A scenic view of the Alps").
Destination Sections:

Create three sections, each representing a different travel destination.
Use <h2> for the destination names (e.g., "Paris," "Bali," "New York").
Add a short description (1-2 lines) under each heading about what makes the destination special.
Images for Each Destination:

Add an image for each destination with descriptive alt attributes.
Learn More Links:

Add a link (<a> tag) under each destination's description to redirect the user to a website for more details about that destination.
Use meaningful text for the links (e.g., "Learn more about Paris").
Back to Top:

Add an anchor link at the bottom of the page that, when clicked, scrolls the user back to the top of the page (use a fragment identifier).